            <ArticleTitle>[Using the lesser saphenous vein as graft for coronary revascularization].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>496-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To investigate the possibility of using the lesser saphenous vein as the alternative bypass graft in coronary artery bypasss graft (CABG).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">Seven pieces of lesser saphenous veins of 6 patients were harvested as the single or sequential grafts of CABG procedure with No-touch technique.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The diameter and length of lesser saphaneous vein met the requirement of graft for entire revascularization. All grafts achieved good flow without significant complications.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The lesser saphenous vein graft is an excellent choice for CABG patient who lacks routine grafts as an alternative material.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
